## ExpressRoute circuit

The connectivity layer deploys an ExpressRoute **gateway**. It does not — and
cannot — order the **circuit**: that is a commercial transaction with a carrier,
placed outside Terraform, and the gateway is useless until it completes.

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Circuit name | {{FACTORY-RAW:computed.docErCircuitName}} |
| Service provider | {{FACTORY-RAW:computed.docErServiceProvider}} |
| Peering location | {{FACTORY-RAW:computed.docErPeeringLocation}} |
| Bandwidth | {{FACTORY-RAW:computed.docErBandwidthMbps}} Mbps |

Place the order with these values, then connect the resulting circuit to the
gateway. The peering location is the carrier's meet-me facility, not an Azure
region, and getting it wrong is expensive to unwind — it is the field most worth
re-reading before the order goes in.
#{{ENDIF}}

## What this document is not

It is not a design. It records answers the wizard collected that reach no
Terraform, so the estate team implements what the client actually chose rather
than rediscovering the question. Everything the factory deploys is described by
the rendered configuration itself.
